# 🔍 Real Production Scenarios

---

## Scenario 1 — Pod Stuck in CrashLoopBackOff

### Steps Performed

```bash id="t1gmhn"
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
kubectl logs <pod-name> --previous
```

### Root Cause

* Missing environment variable
* Incorrect database endpoint

### Fix

* Updated ConfigMap
* Restarted deployment

```bash id="c3i8ks"
kubectl rollout restart deployment/<name>
```

---

## Scenario 2 — Deployment Rollout Stuck

### Investigation

```bash id="v9v1zl"
kubectl rollout status deployment/<name>
kubectl get pods
```

### Found

* Readiness probe failure

### Resolution

* Fixed incorrect health endpoint
* Increased initialDelaySeconds

---

## Scenario 3 — Node NotReady

### Checks

```bash id="l6s0qv"
kubectl describe node <node-name>
```

### Root Cause

* CNI plugin failure

### Fix

* Restarted Flannel DaemonSet
* Verified kubelet/containerd status

---

## Scenario 4 — High CPU Usage

### Commands

```bash id="dldaf7"
kubectl top pods
kubectl top nodes
```

### Resolution

* Increased resource limits
* Configured HPA

---

## Scenario 5 — EBS PVC Pending

### Investigation

```bash id="bg48kr"
kubectl describe pvc <pvc-name>
```

### Root Cause

* Missing EBS CSI Driver

### Fix

* Installed EBS CSI Driver
* Verified StorageClass

